       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and may be a typo.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose is too high.** The usual maximum single dose of oral ibuprofen is 800 mg. You ordered 1600 mg, which is twice that.\n- **The daily total is too high.** 1600 mg four times a day comes to 6400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults on prescription is 3200 mg/day, so this is double. At that level, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular events goes up sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Common doses that may be what you meant:**\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1600 mg/day). This may be where the \"1600\" came from.\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2400 mg/day). The top end would be 800 mg four times daily (3200 mg/day).\n\nPlease tell me the correct dose and how often to give it, and I'll enter it right away. If you really did mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order. I'd strongly suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
